Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.81,0:00:06.28,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.28,0:00:08.81,Default,C,0000,0000,0000,,What's the meaning of this, \NLieutenant General Safida?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.81,0:00:11.88,Default,C,0000,0000,0000,,You're the high commander \Nof the Northern Garrison.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.88,0:00:13.95,Default,C,0000,0000,0000,,Why were you the first to flee?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.54,0:00:17.41,Default,C,0000,0000,0000,,Many soldiers are still in \Nthe process of retreating!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.16,0:00:22.50,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,The commanding officer's safety\Nis the highest priority.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.69,0:00:26.54,Default,C,0000,0000,0000,,I see. You're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.54,0:00:30.63,Default,C,0000,0000,0000,,We'll need you to be present at the \Nmilitary tribunal when this is over.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.17,0:00:37.51,Alderamin-internal/narrator,C,0000,0000,0000,,You mustn't die, Solork.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.45,0:00:41.92,Alderamin-internal/narrator,C,0000,0000,0000,,There's something I have to tell you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.03,0:02:17.82,Alderamin-Episode_Title,C,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(650,1)}Ghost Hunter
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.03,0:02:21.24,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Ideally,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.74,0:02:25.87,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,we would've been able to defend the \Nbarricades without having to retreat.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.66,0:02:30.42,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Even if the enemy attacked again\Nafter they pulled back,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.42,0:02:33.00,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,we could have bought half or even a full day.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.71,0:02:37.51,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Is that loss of a day going to prove fatal?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.26,0:02:39.72,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Not particularly.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.34,0:02:41.34,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,However,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.34,0:02:43.39,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,from now on, it depends on the enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.80,0:02:47.89,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,What will the Holy Aldera Army do, \Nnow that they've actually fought us?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.77,0:02:50.79,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Let's wait and see.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.23,0:02:55.57,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Ryttsah!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.57,0:02:57.28,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Such lovely weather!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.28,0:03:00.03,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Jean, a message from our allies\Nin the mountains.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.66,0:03:04.12,Default,Jean,0000,0000,0000,,Syoo!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.12,0:03:06.29,Default,Jean,0000,0000,0000,,That's your brother, all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.29,0:03:08.62,Default,Jean,0000,0000,0000,,He's selected exactly the information I want.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.12,0:03:11.67,Default,Jean,0000,0000,0000,,And this is the most interesting bit:
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.67,0:03:15.17,Default,Jean,0000,0000,0000,,A member of the Igsem family,\Nfamed for its swordplay, is in that army.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.63,0:03:16.72,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.72,0:03:20.67,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Even my brother referred to \Nher skills as "extraordinary."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.05,0:03:24.43,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,She probably is truly extraordinary, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.22,0:03:31.69,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,It may be thanks to her\Nthat we're stuck here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.07,0:03:39.65,Default,N,0000,0000,0000,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.44,0:03:44.16,Default,N,0000,0000,0000,,It's my fault they died.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.58,0:03:46.95,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,No need to apologize.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.74,0:03:50.16,Default,N,0000,0000,0000,,Ikta apologized to me first.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.16,0:03:53.83,Default,N,0000,0000,0000,,I would have you test my faith as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.67,0:04:00.38,Default,N,0000,0000,0000,,You may cut off both my arms.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.87,0:04:04.19,Default,N,0000,0000,0000,,But please let me keep them \Nfor the duration of this battle,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.19,0:04:07.10,Default,N,0000,0000,0000,,so that I may wield a sword!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.06,0:04:09.98,Default,,0000,0000,0000,,S...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.77,0:04:11.93,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Stop it...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.56,0:04:13.77,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Stop it, please!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.77,0:04:14.94,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,That's not right!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.40,0:04:17.19,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,If you do that, then...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.64,0:04:19.82,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Then...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.45,0:04:26.95,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,how am I supposed to forgive myself?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.05,0:04:30.95,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,I didn't want to kill anyone!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.25,0:04:35.71,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,I didn't want to kill people \Nfrom my own country!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.71,0:04:39.17,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,I had no idea that simply becoming a soldier
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.17,0:04:42.92,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,meant you had to fight so many battles\Nwithout any just cause...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.39,0:04:50.72,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,That's the responsibility of the person\Nwho gave the orders,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.72,0:04:52.18,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Sergeant Major Mitcalif.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.02,0:04:55.64,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,All the people you think you killed
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.64,0:04:57.69,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,were actually killed by me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.81,0:05:00.73,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,You did your job splendidly.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.73,0:05:03.44,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,There's no reason you should \Nbe blamed for anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.36,0:05:09.58,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,But doesn't that mean \Nyou'll be punished by God?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.12,0:05:11.08,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.08,0:05:13.08,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I have a commanding officer, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.08,0:05:16.33,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Once we're all dead, he can \Nactually do some work for once.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.67,0:05:22.30,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,So, change of subject...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.30,0:05:25.05,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Have you two seen First Lieutenant Ikta?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.93,0:05:31.85,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,He should just sleep in his own tent.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.85,0:05:35.60,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,He insisted on sleeping on straw today.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.90,0:05:41.40,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Something they gave their lives to protect...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.40,0:05:46.36,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,You don't see it as a platitude \Nor formality either, do you?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.36,0:05:48.74,Default,N,0000,0000,0000,,Ikta, you boor.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.74,0:05:52.66,Default,N,0000,0000,0000,,If you were going to sleep somewhere, \Nyou could have slept in my bed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.66,0:05:54.24,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Wh-What did you say—
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.29,0:05:56.37,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Captain Sazaluf,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.79,0:05:58.62,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,the enemy's on the move!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.21,0:06:00.75,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,They're here, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.82,0:06:05.96,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Another unit of enemies has split off\Nfor the bypass on the right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.96,0:06:08.38,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Approximately 500 mounted units.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.38,0:06:10.59,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,But half of the horses have two riders:
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.59,0:06:13.14,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,a cavalryman and an infantryman behind him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.60,0:06:15.27,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Clever.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.72,0:06:16.56,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.05,0:06:21.40,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,It's a lot faster than just \Nhaving the infantry walk.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.11,0:06:24.32,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Let's send a force to intercept.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.32,0:06:27.70,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,It's obvious they're trying to \Nmake us split our forces,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.70,0:06:29.53,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,but we can only play along.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.53,0:06:33.20,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,So, the question is who we send.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.20,0:06:35.20,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Torway and I will handle it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.20,0:06:37.29,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,It can be Torway and myself as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.21,0:06:39.67,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I'll go.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.67,0:06:45.17,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Well, my reason is pretty sad,\Nbut hear me out.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.84,0:06:50.18,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,To be honest, this battle's been beyond\Nmy ability to handle for a while now.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.76,0:06:52.30,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,If I'm left in charge here,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.30,0:06:54.93,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I'm not sure I can make the right calls.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.93,0:06:58.98,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,And actually, First Lieutenant Ikta \Nand First Lieutenant Yatorishino,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.98,0:07:01.81,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I think it's a bad idea for \Nyou two to leave this place.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.63,0:07:06.53,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,If occupying a fort and fighting a textbook\Nwar of attrition is all that's needed,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.53,0:07:07.94,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,even I can handle that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.66,0:07:12.49,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Makes me a failure as a commanding officer,\Nbut I'm the best man for this.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.20,0:07:15.08,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Please let me go.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.21,0:07:17.79,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.79,0:07:21.08,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I'll leave you to handle the enemies\Non the bypass route,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.08,0:07:24.84,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,but please take Torway and his men.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.42,0:07:26.63,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,You sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.63,0:07:28.76,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,They're our air rifle unit.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.76,0:07:29.84,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,That's exactly why.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.27,0:07:32.18,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,You can do it, right, Torway?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.18,0:07:33.14,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.97,0:07:41.48,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,It's going to be tough for a while,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.48,0:07:44.98,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,but if you follow Ikkun and \NYatori-san, it'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.69,0:07:46.52,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.52,0:07:47.69,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Hang in there.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.69,0:07:50.11,Default,H,0000,0000,0000,,Take care of the western fort, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.49,0:07:51.24,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.45,0:07:59.91,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,He's really changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.91,0:08:03.92,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,He's standing up straighter. \NIt's like he's grown up.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.92,0:08:04.63,Default,H,0000,0000,0000,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.38,0:08:07.38,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,He's a lot different than me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.38,0:08:08.30,Default,H,0000,0000,0000,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.46,0:08:11.09,Default,H,0000,0000,0000,,Matthew-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.09,0:08:13.55,Default,H,0000,0000,0000,,Anything that's taboo in the Aldera religion
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.55,0:08:15.64,Default,H,0000,0000,0000,,would be taboo for the Aldera Army, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.97,0:08:18.01,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Of course—
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.93,0:08:21.27,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.27,0:08:24.77,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,It's a beautiful day for a trip \Nthrough the sky, right, Miara?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.65,0:08:27.98,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,If you've got time to talk,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.98,0:08:29.90,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,finish this up already!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.74,0:08:31.65,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Syah!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.68,0:08:36.99,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,A force of over a hundred \Nis heading for the west.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.45,0:08:38.87,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,I've written that down!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.87,0:08:40.54,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Now let's get back to the surface.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.54,0:08:41.45,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,As fast as we can!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.45,0:08:42.54,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,Right now!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.18,0:08:45.21,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,We can stay up here a for a bit, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.21,0:08:48.54,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,The general finally gave me the okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.21,0:08:52.92,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,As far as anyone else will be told,\NI'm doing this on my own, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.26,0:08:56.89,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,L-Look, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.89,0:08:58.93,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,That accursed thing!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.93,0:09:02.06,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Oh, what is that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.06,0:09:04.06,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Damn that Kioka kid!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.06,0:09:05.81,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I'll arrest him immediately!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.23,0:09:12.57,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,These little acts aren't for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.99,0:09:17.07,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,You don't seem terribly happy\Nabout this, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.07,0:09:21.24,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,It's the Kiokans who feel it's acceptable\N to break the commandments
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.24,0:09:22.83,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,to ensure victory.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.45,0:09:27.37,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,But it's also true that you can't win a fight
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.37,0:09:29.59,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,if you're only trying to look good for God.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.25,0:09:33.84,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I didn't expect them to send a blimp.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.67,0:09:39.85,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Perhaps the Alderan commander\N is more flexible than we thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.06,0:09:43.72,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Attention!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.44,0:09:46.56,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,That's just a recon vessel.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.56,0:09:50.07,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Don't spend all your time \Nstaring up into the sky at it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.07,0:09:53.11,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,We need to look at reality, \Nand at the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.68,0:09:58.70,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Listen, we need to buy \Na minimum of seven days
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.70,0:10:00.87,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,to support the retreat.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.87,0:10:02.58,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,As you can see,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.58,0:10:06.00,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,the fire we set in the forest \Nis starting to burn out.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.50,0:10:09.75,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,The enemy will come through \Nthe burnt-out parts to attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.75,0:10:14.51,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Which means it's clear \Nwhat we have to do, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.51,0:10:17.83,Default,N,0000,0000,0000,,First, restore the wall of flame.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.83,0:10:21.64,Default,N,0000,0000,0000,,Second, repel the enemies as they attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.22,0:10:23.68,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.68,0:10:27.64,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,From now on, we'll need to maintain \Nan adaptive, mobile defense.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.10,0:10:31.15,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I'll be sending a number of you\Nto the appropriate places
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.15,0:10:33.90,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,depending on where the fire's burnt out\Nand what the enemy does.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.90,0:10:36.78,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,We just keep that up for seven days.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.78,0:10:39.91,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,To pull this off, we just need one thing:
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.91,0:10:43.41,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,a scientific stance from you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.11,0:10:48.29,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,For the next seven days,\Nyou must be lazy in the right way.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.83,0:10:50.71,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,You must work when it's time to work,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.71,0:10:52.79,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,and rest when it's time to rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.79,0:10:56.30,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,And seven days later,\Nwhen our mission is complete,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.30,0:10:58.92,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,we'll be heading south for our own retreat.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.73,0:11:03.30,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I don't doubt that future at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.70,0:11:06.31,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,As of this moment,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.60,0:11:09.94,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I am initiating the mobile defense operation!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.64,0:11:13.18,sign_16080_175_Bypass_Route___W,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(700,1)}Bypass Route - Western Fortress
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.40,0:11:16.82,Alderamin-top,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Wow, that's quite the barrier.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.82,0:11:19.99,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Which means... I guess we go to sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.90,0:11:22.95,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,No, wait, you big dummy!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.63,0:11:27.75,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,It doesn't look like we could knock\N that out at night or by surprise.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.75,0:11:30.21,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,We've got the plan Jean gave us, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.91,0:11:32.62,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,You giant Udo tree!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.62,0:11:36.67,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,How many times do I have to tell you \Nnot to pick people up for no reason?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.06,0:11:40.97,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,So they're finally here, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.97,0:11:43.18,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Doesn't look like\Nthey'll attack tonight, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.05,0:11:47.93,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,They'll attack during the day, \Nwhen they can use their air rifles.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.60,0:11:50.52,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Meraize, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.52,0:11:52.19,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,What's going on with the air mortars?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.77,0:11:55.61,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,We brought them down from the mountains,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.61,0:11:57.07,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,but we only have six.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.07,0:11:57.94,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Forgive us.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.98,0:12:00.32,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Well done.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.22,0:12:10.25,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Okay, pour on the oil!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.67,0:12:20.67,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Yeah, at this rate it'll just\N be another five minutes...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.82,0:12:27.22,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Everyone, stop work and focus to our front!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.16,0:12:30.41,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,Fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.87,0:12:33.70,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,So, it's the third day of the mission,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.70,0:12:35.48,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,and our first enemy encounter?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.04,0:12:38.13,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,That about matches my expectations.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.13,0:12:41.88,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Order Matthew's platoon \Nto take a four-hour rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.88,0:12:43.92,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Yatori will take over for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.92,0:12:44.66,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Roger.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.01,0:12:48.93,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,A report from the rear.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.93,0:12:52.29,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,The blimp has been seen \Nnear the eastern forest path.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.29,0:12:53.89,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,The blimp again?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.89,0:12:55.54,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,And at the east?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.54,0:12:56.77,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.77,0:12:59.10,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,There are 300 cavalry below it,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.10,0:13:01.92,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,running across the same area again and again.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.57,0:13:04.30,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,The same area?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.69,0:13:08.05,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I don't know why.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.91,0:13:10.03,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Nana,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.03,0:13:13.37,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,is there possibly an eastern route\N they could take to get around?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.37,0:13:16.69,Default,N,0000,0000,0000,,No, I guarantee there isn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.83,0:13:20.67,Alderamin-internal/narrator,I,0000,0000,0000,,What are they doing, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.09,0:13:25.59,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Enemy unit withdrawing!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.59,0:13:27.84,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,They're pretty passive.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.84,0:13:32.62,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,With 800 men, they could afford \Nto be a little more bold.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.31,0:13:35.47,Alderamin-internal/narrator,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,What are they waiting for?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.47,0:13:36.52,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,Captain,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.14,0:13:41.55,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,I want to deploy my platoon to the rear.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.55,0:13:43.13,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,May I have permission?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.48,0:13:44.90,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,The rear?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.90,0:13:46.13,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.07,0:13:49.14,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,It can't be—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.37,0:13:56.42,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,The Imperial Army's back is wide open.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.42,0:14:00.19,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,When our rifle attack disorients them,\Nour allies will charge.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.08,0:14:02.88,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Line up on the ridge and prepare to fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.50,0:14:04.38,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.49,0:14:16.16,Alderamin-internal/narrator,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,The red-haired Igsem woman.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.08,0:14:19.58,Alderamin-internal/narrator,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Two blades...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.11,0:14:25.34,Alderamin-internal/narrator,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,This isn't the weapon I should be holding.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.65,0:14:29.40,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,We will open fire now.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.32,0:14:34.28,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Aim, fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.66,0:14:40.90,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,An ambush?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.67,0:14:43.90,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Keep firing!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.46,0:14:46.09,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,The enemy is bunched up!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.09,0:14:47.17,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,We can win!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.17,0:14:54.30,Alderamin-flashback,I,0000,0000,0000,,The third day after you \Narrive at the fortress,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.30,0:14:56.51,Alderamin-flashback,I,0000,0000,0000,,or perhaps the fourth day,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.51,0:14:58.96,Alderamin-flashback,I,0000,0000,0000,,Kala Karm will attack the rear\Nwhile the sun is up.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.31,0:15:02.06,Alderamin-flashback,M,0000,0000,0000,,But we haven't seen Kala Karm...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.06,0:15:03.73,Alderamin-flashback,I,0000,0000,0000,,Not once, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.61,0:15:08.25,Alderamin-flashback,I,0000,0000,0000,,That's just because this area \Nmakes it difficult to attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.25,0:15:09.32,Alderamin-flashback,I,0000,0000,0000,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.90,0:15:11.15,Alderamin-flashback,T,0000,0000,0000,,That's right!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.15,0:15:12.72,Alderamin-flashback,T,0000,0000,0000,,The western fortress is different!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.28,0:15:16.28,Alderamin-flashback,I,0000,0000,0000,,This is the chance they've been waiting for.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.83,0:15:20.48,Alderamin-flashback,I,0000,0000,0000,,They'll attack from the rear \Nusing their air rifles.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.50,0:15:25.08,Alderamin-flashback,T,0000,0000,0000,,How should my unit handle them?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.08,0:15:27.63,Alderamin-flashback,I,0000,0000,0000,,First, turn the chess board around.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.63,0:15:30.17,Alderamin-flashback,I,0000,0000,0000,,If you were the Kala Karm commander,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.17,0:15:31.91,Alderamin-flashback,I,0000,0000,0000,,how would you attack the fortress?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.88,0:15:35.47,Alderamin-flashback,I,0000,0000,0000,,By looking for a place around\N150 meters from the fortress,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.47,0:15:38.22,Alderamin-flashback,I,0000,0000,0000,,where I could easily set up a firing line.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.22,0:15:41.17,Alderamin-flashback,I,0000,0000,0000,,Just keep asking yourself that question.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.64,0:15:46.40,Alderamin-flashback,I,0000,0000,0000,,If the enemy attacked like that, \Nhow would you deal with them?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.44,0:15:50.30,Default,T,0000,0000,0000,,I dealt with them like this, Ikkun!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.20,0:15:54.72,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,All forces, retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.41,0:15:57.07,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,The enemy is retreating.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.78,0:16:00.31,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I won't let a single one escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.21,0:16:12.72,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,You're kidding me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.72,0:16:14.20,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,They took out Kala Karm?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.88,0:16:17.05,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,We don't have a choice. We'll attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.05,0:16:20.06,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,The enemy's split their forces\Nto set that ambush.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.02,0:16:23.21,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,I think they'll come right back, though!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.81,0:16:26.46,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,So we knock out the fortress right now!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.35,0:16:28.31,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,They're here!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.31,0:16:31.03,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Good! Everyone, intercept!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.03,0:16:32.72,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Are the air mortars ready?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.44,0:16:36.47,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,The battle at the fort continues,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.47,0:16:39.99,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,but they say there's no risk\Nof falling right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.99,0:16:43.54,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Use the light signals to \Ntell them they did well.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.54,0:16:45.79,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,And that after three more days of defending,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.79,0:16:47.50,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,they are to retreat.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.50,0:16:48.21,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.63,0:16:52.76,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.76,0:16:54.67,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Torway pulled it off, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.59,0:17:01.00,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Yatori Platoon has finished replenishing \Nthe fires in sector two on the west side.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.72,0:17:02.89,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Hey, Yatori.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.89,0:17:03.97,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Good work.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.10,0:17:08.44,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,I figured that would be the case,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.44,0:17:10.31,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,so I brought some for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.73,0:17:13.53,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.53,0:17:14.65,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,So Torway did it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.19,0:17:16.15,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.15,0:17:19.26,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Looks like he managed to\N deal with the Ghosts.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.70,0:17:21.45,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Did he take out the commander?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.87,0:17:23.41,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.41,0:17:26.15,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,His report said they were \Nalmost entirely wiped out.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.71,0:17:28.46,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,But I assume you
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.38,0:17:32.59,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,wanted revenge for Warrant Officer Deinkun?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.25,0:17:34.40,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.51,0:17:37.80,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Either way, Torway wins.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.80,0:17:39.41,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,This time.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.01,0:17:41.26,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.26,0:17:44.35,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,It may be past the time to \Ntalk about winning and losing.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.85,0:17:47.56,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,The power of the air rifles is overwhelming.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.56,0:17:52.42,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Has the age of the sword already passed?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.36,0:17:57.19,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,From Igsem of the Sword\Nto Remeon of the Gun.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.19,0:17:59.61,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,The star of the battlefield changes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.24,0:18:05.79,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I don't think that's a bad thing\Nfor you, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.50,0:18:09.44,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,You bear too many burdens right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.96,0:18:15.21,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,If I told you everything I'd done \Nsince I joined the military
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.21,0:18:18.57,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,was to make the burden on you lighter,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.17,0:18:20.93,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,would you get mad?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.59,0:18:23.72,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,If I can have that as a goal,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.72,0:18:26.31,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,maybe I can forgive myself...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.27,0:18:33.81,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,For breaking my promise with my mom\Nand becoming a soldier.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.48,0:18:36.34,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,I won't get mad.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.69,0:18:40.34,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,But, even if that's true, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.34,0:18:42.49,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,There's still some time.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.20,0:18:46.16,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Use it all to worry about the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.20,0:18:50.14,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I'll help make it so your conclusion
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.14,0:18:52.92,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,leads to a better future.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.58,0:18:56.21,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Until the day comes when\Nyou can hold your head high
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.21,0:18:57.86,Default,,0000,0000,0000,,and be proud of who you are,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.46,0:19:00.36,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I will be by your side.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.31,0:19:10.91,sign_27532_319_Mobile_Defense_O,I,0000,0000,0000,,Mobile Defense Operation - 6th Day
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.77,0:19:10.92,Alderamin-top,I,0000,0000,0000,,Enemy reinforcements?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.27,0:19:13.73,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,They took a very long way around the east,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.73,0:19:16.80,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,and even our allies on the mountain\Ncouldn't see them.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.80,0:19:19.07,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,The east side of the forest...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.07,0:19:21.78,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,That's where that blimp was flying.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.80,0:19:26.31,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,There are supposedly six wagons \Npulling something big.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.78,0:19:28.54,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Something big?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.16,0:19:32.87,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Have our allies find out \Nwhat it is immediately!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.87,0:19:33.79,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.95,0:19:35.94,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.59,0:19:39.70,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,You did well to make it here by sunset.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.93,0:19:46.35,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Begin loading!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.75,0:19:52.27,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Inject sun energy!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.15,0:19:59.82,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,All cannons are ready to fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.72,0:20:01.84,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.95,0:20:11.37,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,What was that noise?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.37,0:20:12.96,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,It was too loud to be mortars!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.62,0:20:15.23,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Ikta, are those...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.06,0:20:30.20,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,The sound of horses?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.14,0:20:33.11,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,But that way is...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.15,0:20:39.34,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Explosive cannons!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.65,0:20:41.84,Default,M,0000,0000,0000,,What's a explosive cannon?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.40,0:20:44.95,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,It's a new weapon the Kioka military has
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.95,0:20:47.85,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,that detonates compressed sun energy\Nto propel a cannon shell.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.72,0:20:53.58,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,It should be something the Holy Army of\NAldera despises even more than blimps.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.14,0:20:59.04,Default,Y,0000,0000,0000,,Those explosive cannons can destroy \Nthe barricades from beyond the flames.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.20,0:21:02.55,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Oh! So, that was it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.30,0:21:08.24,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,I finally get why the cavalry kept running\Nin the same spot under the blimp!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.59,0:21:11.25,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,They were training!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.05,0:21:15.56,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,They used the blimp to record \Nthe paths through the forest,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.25,0:21:19.52,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,and built an obstacle course to mimic it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.90,0:21:23.72,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,Then they memorized the way to \Nbreak through the wall of flames!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.54,0:21:25.97,Default,I,0000,0000,0000,,They got us!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.28,0:21:28.70,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,So the explosive cannons\Nthat were brought to Aldera,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.70,0:21:31.95,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,and never saw any use,\Nare now used like this...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.58,0:21:36.75,Default,Gi,0000,0000,0000,,But the general is going to be\Nvery upset with you again.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.25,0:21:38.67,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Exkyaazy!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.67,0:21:40.48,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,I'll think of an excuse later.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.34,0:21:46.17,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,Come, it's time to make the Empire pay\Nfor keeping us sitting here.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.26,0:21:49.99,Default,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,All forces, to the west!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.05,0:21:56.18,Alderamin-internal/narrator,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,The Imperial Army's desperate attempt\Nto maintain the firewall
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.18,0:21:58.60,Alderamin-internal/narrator,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,was broken by the\NUnsleeping, Shining Officer.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.19,0:22:01.52,Alderamin-internal/narrator,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,There were less than two days left
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.52,0:22:04.57,Alderamin-internal/narrator,Gu,0000,0000,0000,,until the rear guard could retreat.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.12,0:23:40.35,Default,Next time,0000,0000,0000,,Next time: "In a Twilight Empire."
